--- Harmonic oscillator in rapidity ---
  For a diatomic: omega = sqrt(k/mu)
  rapidity(omega) = [rapidity(k) - rapidity(mu)] / 2
  Isotope shift: rap(omega_D) - rap(omega_H) = [rap(mu_H) - rap(mu_D)] / 2
  C-H to C-D: freq ratio = sqrt(1.008/2.014) = 0.707458
  Isotope shift = -599.1 cents (almost exactly a tritone descent!)
  The descent interval: ~ tritone (45/32), 8.9 cents off

